d-scandal narrative or a post-debate shift toward Tafoya could tighten the polling into toss-up territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Tina Smith (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's open Senate seat features Peggy Flanagan and Michele Tafoya after Tina Smith announced her retirement. The state leans Democratic by about three points, and polls through mid-October consistently put Flanagan ahead by three to four, including surveys from Republican-leaning pollsters. Both nominees have raised roughly ten million dollars, but outside groups have spent far more attacking Flanagan than Tafoya, a sign Republicans see a genuine opening.\n\nCoverage has centered on a Minnesota fraud scandal, a testy debate and affordability, and several outlets note Democratic troubles as Republicans eye an opening in the state. Prediction markets still price Flanagan's chances in the high eighties, and most raters call the race Likely Democratic, with a few at Lean Democratic. She remains favored by roughly five points, with real uncertainty from the narrow polling and the open-seat dynamic.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8725, "margin": 5.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7776, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8131, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8217, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7867, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.784, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7719, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7956, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7935, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7758, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8073, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7878, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7863, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.738, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7059, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p